# ADR-MCPS-048 / MCPS-69 — these HITL live-cloud KMS tests are intentionally
# cargo-only (no Bazel target): each is `#![cfg(feature = "…kms…")]` + `#[ignore]`
# and runs ONLY in the manual live-infra lane (`cargo test --features … --
# --ignored` against real AWS/GCP KMS):
#   tests/aws_kms_live_test.rs, tests/aws_kms_delegated_required_live_test.rs,
#   tests/aws_kms_delegated_signing_live_test.rs,
#   tests/aws_kms_delegated_tls_live_test.rs,
#   tests/aws_kms_http_profile_live_test.rs, tests/aws_kms_root_rotation_live_test.rs,
#   tests/gcp_kms_live_test.rs, tests/gcp_kms_delegated_tls_live_test.rs,
#   tests/gcp_kms_delegated_signing_live_test.rs,
#   tests/gcp_kms_delegated_required_live_test.rs,
#   tests/gcp_kms_http_profile_live_test.rs, tests/gcp_kms_root_rotation_live_test.rs
# Each carries `#[ignore]` LIVE tests; the http-profile and delegated-signing files
# ALSO carry non-ignored `*_offline_local_seed` twins, which the cargo
# feature-gated-backends CI job runs on every push (they need no cloud).
# NOTE: gazelle_rust's `generate_from_cargo` mode enumerates test targets from
# Cargo metadata, so `# gazelle:exclude <file>` does NOT suppress them — gazelle
# will always PROPOSE a target for each in `-mode diff`. This is a documented
# advisory-diff false-positive; MCPS-70's staleness gate must allowlist them (and
# not auto-adopt gazelle write output wholesale). Do NOT add Bazel targets here.

